.TH FECLEAREXCEPT 3 "2026-05-03" "Substrate" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
feclearexcept \- clear floating-point exception flags
.SH LIBRARY
Math Library (libm, \-lm)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <fenv.h>
.PP
.BI "int feclearexcept(int " excepts );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR feclearexcept ()
function clears the floating-point exception sticky flags specified by the
bitwise-OR expression
.IR excepts .
.PP
The argument
.I excepts
is a bitwise OR of zero or more of the following macros:
.TP
.B FE_INVALID
Clear the invalid-operation flag.
.TP
.B FE_DIVBYZERO
Clear the division-by-zero flag.
.TP
.B FE_OVERFLOW
Clear the overflow flag.
.TP
.B FE_UNDERFLOW
Clear the underflow flag.
.TP
.B FE_INEXACT
Clear the inexact-result flag.
.TP
.B FE_ALL_EXCEPT
Clear all exception flags (bitwise OR of all the above).
.PP
Passing zero for
.I excepts
is valid and is a no-op.
.PP
On x86, this function clears the corresponding bits in the x87 FPU status word
and, when SSE is available, in the MXCSR register.
.PP
Unlike
.BR feraiseexcept (3),
this function never causes a floating-point trap.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.BR feclearexcept ()
returns zero on success.
A non-zero return value indicates that one or more of the requested flags
could not be cleared (for example, because
.I excepts
contains bits not supported by the implementation).
.SH ERRORS
No errors are defined.
The function does not set
.IR errno .
.SH EXAMPLES
The following example raises a division-by-zero exception, tests for it, and
then clears it:
.PP
.nf
#pragma STDC FENV_ACCESS ON
#include <fenv.h>
#include <stdio.h>

int main(void)
{
    /* Clear all exception flags before the computation. */
    feclearexcept(FE_ALL_EXCEPT);

    volatile double zero = 0.0;
    volatile double result = 1.0 / zero;   /* raises FE_DIVBYZERO */
    (void)result;

    if (fetestexcept(FE_DIVBYZERO))
        printf("Division by zero detected.\\n");

    /* Clear only the division-by-zero flag. */
    feclearexcept(FE_DIVBYZERO);

    if (!fetestexcept(FE_DIVBYZERO))
        printf("Division-by-zero flag cleared.\\n");

    return 0;
}
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fenv (7),
.BR fegetexceptflag (3),
.BR feraiseexcept (3),
.BR fetestexcept (3)
